    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Circumcellĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m.
		cella. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A class of monks</i>, <i>who</i>, <i>without fixed abode</i>, <i>wandered
				about from cell to cell</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug.
				in Psa. 132</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A class of heretics</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 22, 15</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 8, 5, 53</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
